# Security headers for static hosts that read a _headers file (Netlify, Cloudflare Pages).
# Other hosts: set the same headers in the server config. Inline styles were removed (F-37), so style-src has no 'unsafe-inline'
# on any Metis page. Rules are merged by the host and same-named headers are COMBINED, so the Content-Security-Policy is
# attached per path and the paths below do not overlap. /vendor/ketcher/* (the bundled structure editor, EPAM Ketcher
# 3.18.0) gets its own policy because its React UI sets inline style attributes; it is loaded only in a same-origin iframe
# and cannot reach the API with credentials beyond what any same-origin page can (it makes no network requests).
# 3Dmol.js (vendor/) contains one eval( call site and creates blob workers; see README.md before tightening script-src further.
# connect-src 'self' covers the API: it is served on the same origin under /api (see docs/WEB_WIRING.md).
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin

/
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self'; worker-src 'self' blob:; connect-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'
